{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PLAN REVIEWED AND RECORDED — 9 of 11 criteria now evidenced; the APPLY is blocked and needs an operator decision\n\nRe-verified everything against **current `origin/main` (`25ea12c200ae`)**, with the merged fix\n`13e2ea6decc9c62484f80034e28cb96c20448ea2` confirmed an ancestor\n(`git merge-base --is-ancestor` → true). Fresh worktree, nothing reused from the earlier session\nthat planned off a stale tree.\n\n### AC1 / DoD1 — `terraform plan` COMPLETES (live evidence)\n\nCommand, verbatim, from `/tmp/dd30-wt/infra/terraform`:\n\n    AWS_REGION=us-east-1 terraform plan -input=false -no-color -lock=false -out=/tmp/dd30.tfplan\n\nOutcome, verbatim:\n\n    Plan: 6 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy.\n\n    Saved the plan to: /tmp/dd30.tfplan\n\nExit **0**. `templatefile()` evaluates cleanly; the P1 breakage is gone. `-lock=false` was used so\nthe shared remote state was never locked or written.\n\n### AC2 — comments no longer carry an unescaped `${`\n\nRewording (not `$$`-escaping) was the landed fix. On `origin/main`, `user_data.sh` has zero\nunescaped `${` naming an undeclared variable: `$${!PARAMS[@]}` / `$${PARAMS[$name]}` at `:91`,\n`\"$${!PARAMS[@]}\"` at `:117`. The four legitimate `${data_volume_id}` sites (`:25`, `:28`, `:53`,\n`:56`) are intact — `main.tf:63` declares that variable.\n\n### AC3 — the guard, and proof it is NOT vacuous\n\n`scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py`, wired into `make lint` at `Makefile:302`. It finds BOTH\n`templatefile()` call sites (`main.tf:63`, `modules/sso-gate/main.tf:28`) and checks each template\nagainst that call's own variable map; an unresolvable call site is reported and FAILS rather than\npassing quietly. Confirmed by reading the source, not assumed: `EXCLUDED_DIRS` skips `.terraform`;\n`_DIRECTIVE_KEYWORDS` suppresses `if`/`for`/`in`/`else`/`endif`/`endfor`; `_FOR_BINDINGS` admits\n`%{ for k, v in m }` loop-locals; `check_repo` carries those bindings on a `scopes` stack across\nthe template so a later `${k}` in the loop body resolves.\n\nMutation-tested in a **scratch copy** (`/tmp/dd30-mut`), never in the real tree:\n\n| step | seed verified | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| clean copy | — | **exit 0** |\n| restore the real pre-fix file (`git show 13e2ea6…^:infra/terraform/user_data.sh`) | grep confirmed `${!PARAMS[@]}` present at `:92`, `:111` | **exit 1**, exactly 3 findings: `:92:14`, `:92:30`, `:111:46` |\n| remove the seed | — | **exit 0** again |\n| append line-anchored `echo \"seeded mutant ${NOT_A_DECLARED_VAR}\"` | grep confirmed at line 139 | **exit 1**, `:139:21` |\n\nThe 3 findings are exactly the 3 sites this bug names — and note it did **not** flag the *escaped*\n`$${!PARAMS[@]}` earlier on line 111, only the unescaped half at column 46. A naive `${` grep\ncounts the escaped form as broken; this guard does not. `tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py`:\n**19 passed**.\n\n### AC5 — the three `import` blocks: ADOPTED, no STOP condition\n\nThe plan proposes **no action at all** on them, because adoption already succeeded.\n\n    $ terraform state list | grep -i jira\n    aws_ssm_parameter.jira_project\n    aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_plain_seeded[\"/rebar/prod/jira-url\"]\n    aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_plain_seeded[\"/rebar/prod/jira-user\"]\n    aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/jira-api-token\"]\n\nThose are exactly the addresses `ssm.tf:172-185` imports to. `terraform show -json` prior_state\nrecords all three at **version 2 with their real values** (`is_CHANGEME == false`); no value was\nprinted or logged. In `resource_changes` all three are `no-op` — **not destroyed, not recreated,\nnot overwritten**. AC5's STOP condition does not fire.\n\nThis confirms the \"CORRECTION\" comment above and supersedes the original \"APPLY ABORTED\" comment:\nthe four destroys were an artefact of planning from a tree missing `ab885cef6986`, and they are\nabsent from a plan run against current `origin/main`.\n\n### AC6 — BLAST RADIUS, stated in full. It EXCEEDS the ticket's envelope.\n\n`Plan: 6 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy` — per address:\n\n    create  aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.mcp_mem_abort       <-- BEYOND the stated envelope\n    create  aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.mcp_retire_cap      <-- BEYOND the stated envelope\n    update  aws_instance.gerrit                             (user_data, in place)\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude\"]\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex\"]\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot\"]\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-tickets-pat\"]\n\nThree things an operator must weigh before authorising an apply:\n\n1. **Two CloudWatch alarms are created** — `rebar-autodeploy-mcp-mem-abort` (namespace\n   `rebar/host`, metric `mcp_mem_abort`, Sum > 0 over 4 × 900s) and `rebar-autodeploy-mcp-retire-cap`,\n   both with `alarm_actions`. Additive monitoring, low risk, but outside \"the four SSM parameters\n   and the `user_data` in-place update\".\n\n2. **The `user_data` update STOPS AND STARTS the live Gerrit box.** `aws_instance.gerrit` is\n   `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`, currently `running` at `52.3.128.230` (t4g.large).\n   `user_data_replace_on_change` is unset (`false`), so there is no *replacement* — but the AWS\n   provider modifies `UserData` via a stop/start cycle, and `public_ip` / `public_dns` are already\n   planned as `(known after apply)`, which is the visible signature of that. **This is a Gerrit\n   outage and an IP change**, not a no-op. Anything pinned to `52.3.128.230` breaks.\n\n3. **The apply would FAIL PARTWAY on the three `mcp-client-pat-*` creates.** Independently\n   confirmed against live AWS (metadata only, no values read):\n\n       /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude    SecureString  v1  2026-08-25\n       /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex     SecureString  v1  2026-08-25\n       /rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot   SecureString  v1  2026-08-25\n\n   They exist in AWS, they are **not** in terraform state, and — unlike the Jira parameters — they\n   have **no `import` block** (`grep 'to = aws_ssm_parameter' *.tf` returns only the three Jira\n   ones at `ssm.tf:172-185`). The plan JSON shows `overwrite = null` on all four creates, so\n   `PutParameter` goes out with `Overwrite=false` and returns `ParameterAlreadyExists`. The live\n   token values are not at risk of being clobbered — but the apply does not complete.\n   `/rebar/prod/mcp-tickets-pat` does not exist in AWS, so its create is the only clean one.\n\n### AC4 / DoD5 — NOT DONE. `terraform apply` was NOT run.\n\nDeliberately. An apply mutates shared infrastructure, and this one would stop/start production\nGerrit and then fail on `ParameterAlreadyExists`. **No `--force`, no gate override, no apply.**\n\n**Operator decision needed**, and it is a prerequisite the apply cannot be run around: add\n`import` blocks adopting `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-{claude,codex,copilot}`, mirroring\n`ssm.tf:172-185`. `rebar_secrets` already carries `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }`\n(`ssm.tf:97-99`), so adoption preserves the live token values. That is an infra change in its own\nreviewed commit — out of scope for this bug, which is about `templatefile()` — so it is not\nattempted here.\n\n**This ticket therefore CANNOT be certified-closed yet.** 9 of 11 criteria are satisfied and\nevidenced; the 2 that remain are both the apply, which awaits operator approval with the blast\nradius above."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787959028724849001,"uuid":"5a508d34-623c-47be-9f03-23c60e19007f"}